  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0137_18829426d62b.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 259px;\" />Methoxy group increases the pKa of the phenol group - it makes it less acidic. The oxygen atom does indeed exert an electron-withdrawing inductive effect, but the lone pairs on the oxygen cause the exact opposite effect So the methoxy group is an electron-donating group by resonance.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0137_29dace3b3f8b.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 309px;\" /></p>"
